-- title:
--   Spanning set with residue-independent Gauss units on a Hecke leg
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield generated by the ratios of integral forms for $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, and assume $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $\ell \ne p$ be a prime, write $R$ for [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ (M * p) (M * p * ℓ))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield generated by the ratios of integral forms for $\Gamma_1(Mp) \cap \Gamma_0(Mp\ell)$, again an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $\iota : K \to R$ be an $L$-algebra homomorphism which, on underlying Laurent series, is either the identity or the substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$ (the operator [`ModularCurve.qExpand L ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25), multiplication by $\ell$ on exponents). Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ and $U$ a valuation subring of $R$, each characterised by the Gauss condition that $f$ belongs to it precisely when there are power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f \cdot y = x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ after mapping coefficients from $A$ to $L$. Then there exists $n \in \mathbb{N}$ such that, first, $R$ is spanned by $n$ elements $b_1, \dots, b_n$ over the image of $\iota$: every $z \in R$ can be written $z = \sum_i \iota(c_i) b_i$ with $c_i \in K$; and second, there are $u_1, \dots, u_n \in U$ such that for all $c_1, \dots, c_n \in W_0$ with at least one $c_i$ outside the nonunits of $W_0$, the element $\sum_i \iota(c_i) u_i$ is not in the nonunits of $U$. The integer $n$ is only asserted to exist; it is not identified here with the degree of the leg.
--
--   This is the residue-independence statement for the Gauss valuations attached to a degeneracy (Hecke) leg from $X_1(Mp)$ to the curve of level $\Gamma_1(Mp) \cap \Gamma_0(Mp\ell)$: the roof function field is spanned by $n$ elements over the image of the leg, and the Gauss ring upstairs contains $n$ elements which remain independent modulo the maximal ideal over the Gauss ring downstairs. It is used in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.forall_valuationSubring_heckeRoof_gaussCentre_alpha_iff_beta_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.forall_valuationSubring_heckeRoof_gaussCentre_alpha_iff_beta_x1_mul) to show that the Gauss valuation extends uniquely along the leg, a step in the level-lowering analysis of the mod $p$ geometry of $X_1(Mp)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_span_and_residueIndependent_gauss_heckeRoof_x1_mul.lean

